44:["$","article","sideeffects",{"id":"sideeffects","className":"content-panel","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-title","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Side Effects"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"panel-body","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Safety observations"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"The cited 5-Amino-1MQ studies are primarily preclinical. In obese mice, researchers observed changes in body composition when NNMT inhibition was combined with a change in diet. These findings do not establish human benefit or the safety of this preparation."}]}],["$","p","1",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"The pharmacokinetic paper measured the compound after intravenous and oral administration in rats. Rat half-life results do not establish the timing of human subcutaneous exposure."}]}],["$","p","2",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Those papers cannot provide a reliable rate of headache, jitteriness, local reactions, or long-term adverse effects in people. Calling the compound generally well tolerated in humans would go beyond the evidence they supply."}]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","$1","1",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Reading Animal Studies Without Overextending Them"}],null,[["$","p","0",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"Diet was part of the experiment, not background noise. The mouse study compared NNMT inhibition plus a lean-diet substitution with the diet change alone. Its result belongs to that model and comparison."}]}],["$","p","1",{"children":["$","span",null,{"children":"When comparing a paper with a vial, check the species, compound form, route, and diluent before considering the outcome. A mechanism involving NAD+ does not, by itself, justify adding other compounds to a human regimen."}]}]],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}]
